    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the derived `checkDigit`.\n\n**New/changed domain logic**\n- **`model/MemberId.java`** (new) \u2014 owns the whole identity: `of(region, fy, telephone, lastName)` builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone+lastName`, the same hash the region-and-hash identity used; CHK = Luhn over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`). It also carries `deduplicate(...)` and `regionOf(...)`, which strips the fixed-width `FY+HASH8+CHK` tail (and any dedup suffix) to read REGION back out.\n- **`model/CustomerCode.java`** deleted.\n- **`Luhn`/`Sha256`** javadocs updated to reference the member id.\n\n**Pipeline** (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`)\n- Replaced `assignCustomerCode \u2192 deduplicateCustomerCode \u2192 assignMembershipNumber` with `assignMemberId \u2192 deduplicateMemberId`. Collision handling now applies to the `memberId`. `AssignMemberId`/`DeduplicateMemberId` are new; the three old function classes were deleted.\n\n**Owner entity**\n- Dropped `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` fields and `getCheckDigit()`; added `memberId` (column `member_id`). `getPrimaryIdentifier()` and `getLocality()` now derive from `memberId`.\n\n**Downstream references**\n- Repositories: `findByCustomerCode` \u2192 `findByMemberId` (interface, Spring Data query, JPA, JDBC).\n- Audit: `AuditOwnerCreated` log line now records `memberId`; `OwnerCreatedEvent`'s field renamed to `memberId` (still sourced from `getPrimaryIdentifier()`).\n- `openapi.yml`: removed the three schema fields, added `memberId`, fixed the `locality` description.\n- DB schemas (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres): the two columns replaced by `member_id`.\n\nThe acceptance test's audit output confirms the shape: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (NSW + FY `27` + HASH8 `16E6609E` + CHK `1`).",
